corral: MongoDB wire-protocol connection pooling proxy
Usage: corral [--<setting>=<value> ...]

admin.listen
  flag:    --admin.listen=<value>
  env:     CORRAL_ADMIN_LISTEN
  type:    hostport
  default: 127.0.0.1:9187
  Admin HTTP listener address.

log.format
  flag:    --log.format=<value>
  env:     CORRAL_LOG_FORMAT
  type:    enum (json, text)
  default: json
  Log output format.

log.level
  flag:    --log.level=<value>
  env:     CORRAL_LOG_LEVEL
  type:    enum (debug, info, warn, error)
  default: info
  Minimum log level.

tracing.enabled
  flag:    --tracing.enabled=<value>
  env:     CORRAL_TRACING_ENABLED
  type:    bool
  default: false
  Enable OTLP tracing.

tracing.sample_ratio
  flag:    --tracing.sample_ratio=<value>
  env:     CORRAL_TRACING_SAMPLE_RATIO
  type:    float
  default: 1.0
  Trace sampling ratio.

Control flags (no value allowed):
  --help, -help, -h                print this help and exit
  --version, -version              print the version and exit
  --check-config, -check-config    validate the configuration and exit

OTEL_* environment variables are honoured as described in the operator documentation.
